+// WEBKIT_INDEPENDENT_SCROLL: fully separate scrolling from the main-thread
+// rendering update, the way Gecko/APZ (and the EmbedLite port) do it.
+//
+// Upstream's design is a *conditional* desync: on every display refresh the
+// scrolling thread blocks on m_stateCondition for up to half a frame waiting for
+// the main thread to finish its rendering update, and only when that times out is
+// it allowed to write scroll offsets into the compositor scene itself
+// (SynchronizationState::Desynchronized). So every single scroll frame pays a
+// main-thread latency tax, and a main thread that is merely slow -- not stuck --
+// still drags the scroll with it.
+//
+// The machinery to scroll without the main thread already exists and is exercised
+// (that Desynchronized path); this flag simply makes it the default rather than a
+// timeout fallback:
+//   1. the scrolling thread applies layer positions + requests an AsyncScrolling
+//      composite on EVERY refresh, regardless of the synchronization state;
+//   2. willStartRenderingUpdate() no longer round-trips through the scrolling
+//      thread (main thread stops blocking on a BinarySemaphore, scrolling thread
+//      stops waiting on m_stateCondition);
+//   3. synchronous-scrolling reasons no longer veto scrolling-thread layer
+//      updates -- WEBKIT_FORCE_ASYNC_SCROLL already accepts that trade-off for
+//      the dispatch path, and vetoing here is inconsistent with it.
+//
+// Nothing in the compositor needs the main thread to recomposite an already
+// committed scene: requestComposition(AsyncScrolling) reaches renderLayerTree with
+// no main-thread involvement, and m_isWaitingForRenderer only gates composites
+// whose reason is RenderingUpdate.
+//
+// Deliberately lossy, same bargain as APZ: scroll-linked JS and `scroll` events
+// fire at main-thread cadence rather than per frame, and content newly scrolled
+// into view is only painted once the main thread runs, so a slow page shows more
+// low-res/checkerboard tiles while scrolling instead of freezing.
+static bool independentScrollEnabled()
+{
+    static bool enabled = [] {
+        const char* env = getenv("WEBKIT_INDEPENDENT_SCROLL");
+        return env && *env && strcmp(env, "0");
+    }();
+    return enabled;
+}
+
 bool ThreadedScrollingTree::canUpdateLayersOnScrollingThread() const
 {
+    if (independentScrollEnabled())
+        return true;
+
     return !m_hasNodesWithSynchronousScrollingReasons;
 }
 
